{
  "_note": "Tier-1 reactivity feedback matrix (M3-GAME-01 / AUTH #022, SPEC §3.6). The authoritative, declarative mapping the Unity shader-displacement + particle system consumes: per scene_graph MATERIAL, how a surface reacts (displacement kind + stiffness + default particle); per gameplay EVENT (verb/tool/landing/reaction), what it triggers (particle, haptic, camera shake, and whether it displaces the surface). Keyed off the frozen scene_graph material enum and the traversal_graph verb enum, so it shares one source of truth with the audio bank. Shader displacement only (Tier 1) -- NO physics (Tier 2 is research, SPEC §5). All reactions scale by the environment multiplier so a tiny world's dust/dents stay tiny. Particle/haptic/shake also feed Tier 0 (M1-GAME-03).",
  "displacement_kinds": ["none", "dent", "sway", "flutter", "swing"],
  "particle_kinds": ["none", "dust", "grit", "lint", "petal", "spark", "splinter", "scuff"],
  "haptic_levels": ["none", "light", "medium", "heavy"],
  "shake_levels": ["none", "light", "heavy"],
  "material_response": {
    "wood": { "displacement": "none", "stiffness": 0.90, "particle": "grit" },
    "tile-stone": { "displacement": "none", "stiffness": 1.00, "particle": "grit" },
    "carpet-rug": { "displacement": "dent", "stiffness": 0.40, "particle": "lint" },
    "fabric-cushion": { "displacement": "dent", "stiffness": 0.20, "particle": "lint" },
    "lego-plastic": { "displacement": "none", "stiffness": 0.95, "particle": "none" },
    "paper-cardboard": { "displacement": "flutter", "stiffness": 0.30, "particle": "none" },
    "metal": { "displacement": "none", "stiffness": 1.00, "particle": "spark" },
    "glass": { "displacement": "none", "stiffness": 1.00, "particle": "none" },
